 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law and the\npublic authorities law, in relation to racing at Belmont Park",
    "basePrintNo": "S8985",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8985-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§206 & 212, RWB L; amd §§1676 & 1680, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8985\n\nSPONSOR: PHILLIPS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law and\nthe public authorities law, in relation to racing at Belmont Park\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation enables NYRA to obtain the financing necessary to reno-\nvate Belmont Park with 21st century amenities and, once again, transform\nthe property into the world-class racing facility it has been in the\npast.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1. Subdivision 2 of section 206 of the racing, pari-mutuel wagering\nand breeding law, as amended by chapter eighteen of the laws of 2008, is\namended to, subject to Franchise Oversight Board (FOB) approval, extend\nNYRA's right and responsibility to manage and operate all functions at\nBelmont Park until December thirty-first, two thousand sixty eight.\n\n§ 2. Subparagraph (viii) of paragraph 8 of subdivision a of section 212\nof the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law is amended to,\nsubject to FOB approval, extend NYRA's ground lease for Belmont Park\nuntil December thirty-first, two thousand sixty eight.\n\n§ 3. Paragraph (b) of subdivision 2 of section 1676 of the public\nauthorities law is amended by adding a new undesignated paragraph to\nread as follows: The New York Racing Association, Inc. for capital\nprojects.\n\n§ 4. Subdivision 1 of section 1680 of the public authorities law is\namended by adding a new undesignated paragraph to read as follows:  The\nNew York Racing Association, Inc. for capital projects.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNYRA intends to renovate Belmont Park with 21St century amenities and,\nonce again, transform the property into the world-class racing facility\nit has been in the past. To fund the redevelopment, NYRA will need to\npursue financing options. Under current law, NYRA's right to manage and\noperate Belmont Park and the corresponding ground lease extend only\nuntil December 31, 2033. Such a term does not allow NYRA to secure the\nnecessary financing for these renovations. NYRA desires legislation\nextending, subject to FOB approval, NYRA's right to manage and operate\nBelmont Park and the corresponding ground lease until December thirty-\nfirst, two thousand sixty eight.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect in thirty days, provided, however, that the\nstate shall immediately take all steps necessary to amend the franchise\nagreement dated as of September twelfth, two thousand eight by and among\nthe franchise corporation, the state, and the franchise oversight board\nto reflect the amendments made to the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and\nbreeding law, made by section 1 of this act; and the franchise oversight\nboard shall immediately amend the ground lease for Belmont Park entered\ninto by the state and through the franchise oversight board as lessor\nand the franchised corporation as lessee, dated September twelfth, two\nthousand eight, to reflect the amendments made to the racing, pari-mutu-\nel wagering and breeding law, made by section 2 of this act.\n",
