    "lawCode": "Amd §1676, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8985A\n\nSPONSOR: PHILLIPS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the New York\nRacing Association, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation enables NYRA to obtain the financing necessary to reno-\nvate Belmont Park with 21st century amenities and, once again, transform\nthe property into the world-class racing facility it has been in the\npast.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\n§ 1. Paragraph (b) of subdivision 1676 of the public authorities law is\namended by adding a new undesignated paragraph to read as follows:  The\nNew York Racing Association, Inc. for capital projects.\n\n§ 2. Subdivision 1 of section 1680 of the public authorities law is\namended by adding a new undesignated paragraph to read as follows:  The\nNew York Racing Association, Inc. for Capital projects.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNYRA intends to renovate Belmont Park with 21st century amenities and,\nonce again, transform the property into the world=class racing facilitiy\nit has been in the past. To fund the redevelopment, NYRA will need to\npursue financing options. This bill would authorize NYRA to obtain\nfinancing and construction services through DASNY for this redevelopment\nproject, as well as other capital projects at all three NYRA racetracks.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
